      "side": 1,
      "message": "I successfully tested the output of the following logs comparing the log4j 2.x output with the output of the old log4j 1.x implementation\n- error_log, error_log.json\n- httpd_log, httpd_log.json\n- sshd_log, sshd_log.json\n- delete_log, delete_log.json\n- replication_log, replication_log.json\n- gc_log\n\nI could also successfully list, set and reset loggers via the corresponding ssh commands.\n\nThat\u0027s great, thanks :-)\n\nBut I think the way the `Configuration` is modified at runtime is violating the recommendations given in the log4j 2.x documentation. We should not modify the existing active `Configuration` object but we should instead build a new one and then use the `LoggerContext.reconfigure(Configuration)` method to atomically switch from the old to the new configuration.\n\nAs soon as this change landed we need to adapt more plugins and lib modules to log4j 2.x which depend on the log4j API:\n- event-broker\n- global-refdb\n- loglevel\n- rename-project\n- spanner-refdb\n(these are the ones we use, I guess there are more)",
      "revId": "fc9c28f032cef5ed0b67f2f43c563d5f14c2eb8f",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
