      "writtenOn": "2025-09-10T13:16:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "the documentation recommends to create a new Configuration and use `Configurator.reconfigure(Configuration)` to reconfigure the active `LoggerContext` with a different `Configuration`:\n\n```\nConfiguration configuration \u003d createConfiguration();\nConfigurator.reconfigure(configuration);\n```\n\nsee https://logging.apache.org/log4j/2.x/manual/customconfig.html#Configurator\nand https://logging.apache.org/log4j/2.x/manual/architecture.html#reconfiguration\n\nThere is also a `reconfigure` method on `LoggerContext`:\nhttps://logging.apache.org/log4j/2.x/javadoc/log4j-core/org/apache/logging/log4j/core/LoggerContext.html#reconfigure(org.apache.logging.log4j.core.config.Configuration)\n\nAFAIU the `reconfigure` methods are atomic. When reconfigure is called log events which are already being processed will continue to write log using the old configuration and those started after the transaction was committed will use the new configuration. Hence I think we should avoid modifying the old active `Configuration` object to be swapped with the new object.",
      "revId": "fc9c28f032cef5ed0b67f2f43c563d5f14c2eb8f",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "61212f67_608751ab",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/pgm/http/jetty/HttpLog.java",
