      "writtenOn": "2025-09-10T13:16:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The documentation strongly advises against programmatically modifying components of the active `Configuration`! \n\nIt seems the log4j2 maintainers favour an approach where the client has to create a new modified `Configuration` object from scratch, e.g. using `ConfigurationBuilder` which is then swapped with the old configuration using the above mentioned `reconfigure` methods. I couldn\u0027t find a deep copy method for `Configuration`. Maybe we need to roll our own ?\n\nSee https://logging.apache.org/log4j/2.x/manual/customconfig.html#Hybrid",
      "revId": "fc9c28f032cef5ed0b67f2f43c563d5f14c2eb8f",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
